  Cell["2.3 Singlet and triplet channels: Proposition (chi-pp)", 
   "Subsection"], Cell["chi_pp,ss'(nu, nu', omega) = chi_ss'(nu, nu', -omega \
- nu - nu'): the ph transfer becomes w -> -wpp - vn - vm, the ph delta_(k0) \
becomes the pp mirror delta_(m, -n-k-1), and delta_(nn') stays. With the pp \
bubble B = -beta/2 G(nu) G(-nu - omega), chi_s = (-chi_pp,upup + 2 \
chi_pp,updn - 2 B)/4 and chi_t = (chi_pp,upup + 2 B)/4. Each has a generic \
part, a diagonal part (\"dd\") and a mirror part (\"mir\", evaluated on the \
mirror vm = -vn - wpp).", "Text"], 
  Cell[BoxData[{RowBox[{RowBox[{RowBox[{"toPP", "[", "f_", "]"}], " ", ":=", 
         " ", RowBox[{"f", " ", "/.", " ", RowBox[{"w", " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", "wpp"}], " ", "-", " ", "vn", " ", "-", 
               " ", "vm"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
     RowBox[{RowBox[{"mirror", " ", "=", " ", 
