  Cell["6.4 Step 3: pole pairs", "Subsection"], 
  Cell["phi(t) = fp/(t - u) + fm/(t + u). Its image under P(z) chi_r: -beta \
H(z) phi(z), lambda C phi = lambda [fp alpha(u)/(z + u) + fm alpha(-u)/(z - \
u)], and fp I(z; u) + fm I(z; -u) with I = Ibar + alpha N/(rho P). Write al = \
alpha(u); then alpha(-u) = h^2/al (Section 5). The residues at z = u and z = \
-u vanish together iff beta^2 H(u) H(-u) - lambda^2 h^2 = beta^2 e(u) = 0. \
Choose the null vector fp = beta H(-u), fm = lambda al of the second residue. \
The claim, Eq. (mode-image): at a root u of e (for m, k = 0 at the non-atomic \
roots; the atomic root u^2 = a^2 is a double zero of P and is not needed, see \
below), the image is -beta K [z + W(z; u^2)/(rho P(u))] with K = beta H(-u) + \
lambda al. Check: the numerator of (image - claim) is divisible by e(u) as a \
polynomial in u.", "Text"], 
